<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#khowar-language">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khowar language</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chitrali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khowar, also called Chitrali, is an Indo-Aryan language of the Dardic group spoken by several hundred thousand people in Chitral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-frontier-province">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, and in parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgit-baltistan">Gilgit-Baltistan</a>. It was the main language of the people and court of the princely state of Chitral under the Mehtars, and it is written in a form of the Perso-Arabic script.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khowar-language.jpg" alt="Khowar language" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThatDohDude · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khowar_in_Perso-Arabic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
